# What EAS leaves OUT of the archive it uploads to build.
#
# THIS FILE BELONGS AT THE REPO ROOT, not in mobile/. The Expo project is
# mobile/, but the archive is rooted where git is — here — so a .easignore
# under mobile/ does not govern it.
#
# CAREFUL: when this file exists, EAS uses it INSTEAD OF .gitignore, not on top
# of it. Everything .gitignore says has to be repeated, or node_modules, the
# generated native folders and the secrets below all get uploaded. Keep the two
# in step; the only intended difference is the `mobile/store/` block at the end.

# ── Secrets / env ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env
*.pem
*.p8
*.p12
*.jks
*.key
*.mobileprovision
*.keystore

# ── Node ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# ── Expo / React Native ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts
.metro-health-check*

# Generated native folders. EAS runs its own prebuild; shipping a populated
# android/ would make it build the locally-generated project instead.
/mobile/ios/
/mobile/android/

# ── TypeScript ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Supabase local dev ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
supabase/.branches/
supabase/.temp/
supabase/test/

# ── Build artifacts / logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.apk
*.aab
*.ipa
*.log

# ── Store pack ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
mobile/store/apple-review/

# ── Editor / OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.orig.*
.vscode/
.idea/

# ── Claude / assistant metadata ────────────────────────────────────────────
# .claude/ holds .claude/secrets/google-play.json, the Play service account
# key. It must never reach a build machine.
.claude/
.mcp.json
.agents/
skills-lock.json

.vercel
.env*

# ── Signing credentials pulled down with `eas credentials` ─────────────────
# credentials.json holds the keystore and key PASSWORDS in plaintext. A cloud
# build must never receive them: EAS holds the keystore server-side and signs
# with it there. (*.jks above already covers the keystore itself.)
mobile/credentials.json
mobile/credentials/

# ── The only thing this file adds over .gitignore ──────────────────────────
# Store listing artwork and screenshot sources: tracked in git (real work), but
# no build reads them, and they are ~79 MB of the upload.
mobile/store/
